            <ArticleTitle>Arthrocentesis and therapeutic joint injection: an overview for the primary care physician.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>691-702, v</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.pop.2010.07.002</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Athrocentesis and therapeutic joint injection is a safe and useful primary care procedure. Fluid collection and analysis from effused joints is important to establish a cause and therefore inform appropriate management. Therapeutic joint injection can give patients significant, rapid, localized pain relief.</AbstractText>
